# cli — the product as a toolbox binary

This product's `main.go` calls `cli.Main(Modules()...)`, so the binary is a
toolbox: subcommands collected from the graph.

- Built in: `serve` (default), `routes`, `graph`, `blast`, `doctor` (support
  bundle + every `cli.DoctorInfo`), plus `config reference` from conf and
  `openapi`/`client` from api.
- Add a command by providing `cli.Command` from any module. `Boot: true` for
  commands needing live components (starts ONLY their dependency closure);
  `Destructive: true` demands `--yes`; `Remote: true` runs inside the live
  instance over the admin socket ($TMPDIR/<app>.sock).
- Every builtin honors global `--json`. Write output via `cli.Stdout(ctx)` and
  support --json with `cli.Emit(ctx, data, humanFn)`. Test in-process:
  `code, out, errOut := cli.Test(args, Modules()...)`.

Framework reference (generated): ultrastack `references/presets/cli.md`.
